  "notes": "Clementi Op. 36 No. 1, first movement, exposition bars 1-15, ending on the cadence in G (dominant key). The old repo melody was not Clementi's opening. Original meter is alla breve 2/2 (tag says 4-4; kept 4/4, durations identical). LH is Clementi's: mostly single bass quarters, with the eighth-note figures in bars 4, 9, 11 and 15 (checked against the gmajormusictheory engraving). Final G4 half note held through the closing half-bar rest so the excerpt ends on a full bar. Validation exceptions (intermediate): D6 in bar 12 is 2 semitones above the RH range, composer's peak note; F# is the modulation to G."
